From b666ed36240ef5736faab8b1b1ca2235bcdca8d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:40:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 79/80] mir: a borrow into the middle of a static is a borrow
 of the field or element there

rug 1.28.1 src/integer/big.rs `Integer::ONE`:

    pub const ONE: &'static Integer = {
        const MINI: MiniInteger = MiniInteger::const_from_bool(true);
        const BORROW: BorrowInteger = MINI.borrow();
        BorrowInteger::const_deref(&BORROW)
    };

    MIR ERROR: ::rug::lifted#C_21 BB0/0: src/mir/cleanup.cpp:461 ASSERT ofs == 0 failed
    - TODO: Support offset pointers in borrows - +0xc

`MiniInteger::borrow` points `mpz_t::d` at `self.limbs`, so the evaluated `BORROW`
holds a pointer 0xc bytes (0x10 on 64-bit) into the static that holds `MINI`. Constant
evaluation and static emission already handle that offset (`(uintptr_t)&sym+12`).
When MIR cleanup turned the constant back into MIR for a body that uses it (here the
lifted `&BORROW`), `MIR_Cleanup_LiteralToRValue` only accepted pointers to the start of
a static.

For a thin pointer, walk from the static's type to the struct/tuple field or array
element starting at that offset (using the same `Target_GetTypeRepr` layout that
produced the offset) and borrow that place through the static's address, so the
result is `&(*&STATIC).1[0]` and not integer arithmetic, which constant evaluation
can't follow. A type mismatch at the end gets the same pointer casts as before.
An offset that lands inside a primitive, enum or union, or a slice or trait-object
pointer with an offset, still reports a TODO.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
